<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Consent's cross-section surface as its own leaf project: a Contracts/ *folder* inside
    Humans.Consent would make consumers reference the section and risk cycles (design §15.5b,
    memory/architecture/section-project-cycle-fix.md). Consumers today: Onboarding, Users,
    Governance, Agent, Scanner, and Shell's onboarding widget.

    ILegalDocumentSyncRunner's consumers are now all in-section and it could fold inward;
    ILegalDocumentSyncServiceRead cannot yet (Governance's MembershipCalculator injects it).
    Shrinking contract surface needs Peter.

    ConsentReviewFormViewModel is here for the reason step 3b's "move the markup" case
    does not apply: the onboarding widget's Consents step is Onboarding's view over
    Consent's form, so Shell constructs the model for the section's
    _ConsentReviewBody partial. It names no ASP.NET type.

    Everything with no consumer outside the section stays internal: the admin
    legal-document surface, the GitHub connector, the sync service's write half, the
    consent dashboard, both repositories and all three entities.

    References Humans.Base (IApplicationService, IInvalidator) and NodaTime
    (Instant on the snapshots).
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Base\Humans.Base.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="NodaTime" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
